{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"We divide the numerator and the denominator by $2\\,$ so that the denominator has a constant term of $1\\,$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\displaystyle f(x)= \\frac{1}{2-x}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{1-\\frac{x}{2}}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"This is now a geometric series with first term $a=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\,$ and common ratio $r=\\displaystyle\\frac{x}{2}\\,$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Therefore, the series is as follows.\n\n\n$\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{x^2}{8}+\\ldots +\\frac{x^n}{2^{n+1}}+\\ldots $","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{2-x}$\n\n**Find a power series for $f$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\displaystyle 1+\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{4}x^2+\\ldots +\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^n  x  ^n+\\ldots$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\displaystyle 1-x+x^2+\\ldots +\\left(-1\\right)^n  x  ^n+\\ldots$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\displaystyle 1-x-x^2+\\ldots -x ^n+\\ldots$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{x^2}{8}+\\ldots +\\frac{x^n}{2^{n+1}}+\\ldots$","correct":true}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":true,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
